        <div class="callout green">
          <div class="callout-label" style="color:var(--green);">
            The XSS gap most people miss
          </div>
          <p>
            The XMP stream is a separate XML blob embedded inside the PDF
            binary. Preview, Windows Properties, and pdfinfo do not read it at
            all. Adobe Reader reads parts of it. Only ExifTool and FileIntel
            read the complete XMP stream — which is where GPS coordinates,
            extended author information, and enterprise custom fields are
            typically stored.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:10px;">
            If you are checking a document for sensitive data before sharing, a
            tool that misses XMP gives you false confidence.
          </p>
        </div>

